  "interpretation": "External stability, not internal freshness. A match means the publisher still serves the bytes the manifest recorded; a drift means a fresh run of tools/acquire_corpus.py on this machine would produce a different corpus from the one every published artifact was computed from. Neither result changes any number in this repository: the artifacts are pinned to the recorded hashes, and the tests re-hash those bytes. What a drift changes is what a third party can re-acquire, so the manifest, not the live site, is the authority for this study's measurements.",
  "what_it_does_not_establish": "It does not show the acquired texts are correct, complete or rights-clean; it does not date the edit; and one run is a snapshot, not a monitoring record. Works whose acquired copy is absent because corpus/raw/ is gitignored are reported separately rather than counted as drift."
